## 15. Logging

```python
# infrastructure/logging.py
import structlog

structlog.configure(
    processors=[
        structlog.stdlib.add_log_level,
        structlog.stdlib.add_logger_name,
        structlog.processors.TimeStamper(fmt="iso"),
        structlog.processors.JSONRenderer(),
    ]
)

logger = structlog.get_logger()

# Usage in use cases / services:
logger.info("employee_created", employee_id=str(employee.id), email=employee.email)
logger.error("database_error", error=str(exc), operation="save_employee")
```

Never use `print()` in production code. Use structured logging (structlog).

