## Anti-Patterns

These patterns are **never acceptable**. The AI MUST reject, refactor, or flag them when encountered.

| Pattern | Why | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| `.dict()` on Pydantic v2 models | Deprecated in v2; will be removed | `.model_dump()` |
| Business logic in FastAPI route functions | Untestable without HTTP setup | Move to application service / use case |
| Mixing sync and async functions in the same call chain | Blocks the event loop | Keep async throughout; use `asyncio.to_thread` for sync I/O |
| `except Exception: pass` | Silent failures; impossible to debug | Log with `logger.exception(...)`, re-raise or map |
| SQLAlchemy `session.execute()` without `await` in async mode | Blocks event loop | `await session.execute(...)` |
| Hardcoded credentials or DSNs | Config leaks; breaks env portability | `pydantic-settings` with env vars |
| `response_model=None` on endpoints that return data | No schema validation or OpenAPI docs | Always define `response_model` |
| Bare `raise` in FastAPI route without `HTTPException` | Returns 500 with raw traceback | Raise `HTTPException` or use global exception handler |
